# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA — never commit.
# The ITSM exports contain employee names, employee IDs, email addresses and
# full ticket bodies. None of it belongs in version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.tsv
*.pdf
*.docx
data/
exports/
uploads/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — never commit.
# .clasp.json holds the Apps Script project ID that links this folder to your
# Google account. Keep it local; .clasp.json.example shows the shape.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.clasp.json
.clasprc.json
*.env
credentials.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# The harness page is assembled from src/ by tests/harness/build.js. It is a
# build artifact - half a megabyte that changes on every edit to any source
# file - so it is rebuilt rather than committed.
tests/harness/page.html

# Screenshots rendered from the harness to show a change before it is pasted
# into Apps Script. Same reasoning as the page above: generated, and stale the
# moment anything is edited.
preview/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
